            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is not an issue with 'mini.hues' (or any color scheme, for that matter). This is the effect of tree-sitter highlighting: as it is done with extmarks, if highlight group defines background color, it is used on top of the cursorline. You can check which highlight group overrides cursorline by executing `:Inspect` in the target range.",
